            <zone h='2134' id='374' type-v2='empty' w='98858' x='571' y='7200'>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone fixed-size='1352' h='90133' id='113' is-fixed='true' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98858' x='571' y='9334'>
              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='88533' id='176' type-v2='text' w='98858' x='571' y='9334'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>What is Metric Drift?</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>A metric is considered to be “drifting” when it shows an </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' italic='true'>abrupt</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> deviation from its recent behavior </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' italic='true'>(over the past 7 days)</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> and starts producing </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>abnormal</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> or </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>unexpected</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> values. This often indicates issues such as data pipeline failures, logic changes, or broken inputs, all of which can </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>negatively impact the performance of rules and models</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Dashboard Objective:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Early detection</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> of metric drift affecting fraud rules to reduce false positives, review/decline spikes, and business impact.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>What&apos;s in the Dashboard?</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     A) </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' underline='true'>Metric Drift Detection Logic:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>           1. Drift Indecators:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                • </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Average Value Shift: </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>Change in Avg value over time</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                   - </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Z-score &gt; 3</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                   - AND Avg % Change &gt; 50%</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                • </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Data Range Shift: </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>Change in data range over time</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                   - IQR % Change &gt; 50% -- </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>(IQR = </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>middle 50%</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'> of the data = P75 - P25)</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                   - OR Spread % Change &gt; 50% -- </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>(Spread = </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>middle 80%</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'> of the data = P90 - P10)</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run italic='true'>Æ     </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>           2. Drift Severity:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                • </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>High:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> Both drift indicators are met</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                • </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Medium:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> One indicator is met, with a slightly higher threshold (Z-score &gt; 4, IQR/Spread &gt; 100%)</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                • </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Low:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> One indicator is met</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     B) </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' underline='true'>Additional Info:</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' italic='true'>Supporting information to help understand the broader context and impact of drift.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>          1.</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> Rule List:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> Rules that use the metric</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>          2. </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Global Entity List:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> All global entities in which the meric is used</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>          3. </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Metric Update Info:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> Changes to the metric (e.g. new version created, version deleted/deactivated)</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>          4. </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Business Impact:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>               a) </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>: Change in total friction (Decline, Review, or Approve) caused by rules using the drifted metric</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>               b) </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Share of Total Region Friction:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> The portion of total regional friction caused by rules that use the drifted metric</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     C) </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' underline='true'>Alerts:</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' italic='true'>Not every drift triggers an alert. Alerts appear only when there’s a combination of signals — either widespread drift or proven business impact.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>          Alert Types:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>               • </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Incident Alert:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                   - P0: </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>When &gt;10 metrics are flagged with </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>High</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> drift severity on the same day (region-agnostic) -- </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>Alert Message: &quot;Widespread High Metric Drift; x metrics flagged.&quot;</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>                   - P1: </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>When &gt;10 metrics are flagged with </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Medium</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> drift severity on the same day (region-agnostic)</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>               • </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Individual Alerts:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                  Triggers based on drift severity, rule impact, and share of region total friction -- and </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' italic='true'>only if NO Incident Alert is triggered</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                  - P0:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>High </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Drift + </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>&gt;100% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>&gt;20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> -- </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>Alert Message: &quot;High possibility of Metric Drift, High impact on rules and region’s total friction.&quot;</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>                  - P1:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Medium</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> Drift +  </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>&gt;100% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>&gt;20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                  - P2:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>High</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> drift + </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>&gt;100% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>≤20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> -- </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>Alert Message: &quot;High possibility of Metric Drift, High impact on rules friction, Little to no impact on region’s total friction.&quot;</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>                  - P3:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Medium</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> drift + </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>&gt;200% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>≤20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>                  - P4: High</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> drift + </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>≤100% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>≤20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>                  - P5:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Medium</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> drift + </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>≤100% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>≤20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Notes:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     1. The dashboard is </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>region-agnostic</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> — each region is evaluated independently.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     2. The current definitions and thresholds for drift signals, severity levels, and alerts are subject to change based on alignment with stakeholders.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     3. Whenever % change is mentioned here, it typically refers to a comparison between the current value and the past 7 days.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     4. We consider </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>absolute change</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>, so both increases and decreases are captured.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     5. We’ve tested multiple detection approaches with varying thresholds (Aggressive, Conservative, and More Conservative). As aligned, the current dashboard uses the </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Aggressive</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> approach. This may change with future alignment. Further details can be found here &gt;&gt;&gt; </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>(</run>
                  <run auto-url='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1icQOXH61OJyCo0CqHQAENcfWw3jyFh1-NCH8VDtsNCk/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;'>https://docs.google.com/document/d/1icQOXH61OJyCo0CqHQAENcfWw3jyFh1-NCH8VDtsNCk/edit?usp=sharing</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>)</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     6. Similarly, alerting is currently limited to </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>High drift</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> only. Therefore, for </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Incident Alerts</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>, only </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>P0</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> will appear. For </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Individual Alerts</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>, only </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>P0</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> and </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>P2</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> are shown.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     7. Incident Alerts take precedence over Individual Alerts. For a given region and day, only one type of alert can be triggered. We first check for an Incident Alert; if none, we then check for an Individual Alert.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'><![CDATA[     8. Region here refers to the “cluster” the entity is added to in Antifraud — it doesn’t necessarily match the geographic region, or the platform name. Mapping source is <]]></run>
                  <run fontcolor='#080808' fontsize='11'>fulfillment-dwh-production.cl_fintech.antifraud_metric_definition</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>&gt;.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Source Table:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'><![CDATA[ <fulfillment-dwh-production.rl_fintech.agg_antifraud_metrics_drift_daily>]]></run>
                </formatted-text>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='424' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='98934' id='423' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98858' x='571' y='533'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='6667' id='23' type-v2='text' w='81001' x='571' y='533'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#050038' fontname='Tableau Semibold' fontsize='20'>Information</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Light'>Owner: </run>
                    <run fontname='Tableau Light'>Fintech Data - Risk Analytics (fintech_risk_analytics@deliveryhero.com)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Light'>Designed By:</run>
                    <run fontname='Tableau Light'> Daniel Lima de Souza (daniel.lima@deliveryhero.com)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Light'>Update Schedule:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontname='Tableau Light'>Daily at 4pm CET</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone fixed-size='92' h='6667' id='323' is-fixed='true' is-scaled='1' param='Image/DH_Fintech_Full_RGB.png' type-v2='bitmap' w='17857' x='81572' y='533'>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='88533' id='176' type-v2='text' w='98858' x='571' y='9334'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>What is Metric Drift?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>A metric is considered to be “drifting” when it shows an </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' italic='true'>abrupt</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> deviation from its recent behavior </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' italic='true'>(over the past 7 days)</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> and starts producing </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>abnormal</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> or </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>unexpected</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> values. This often indicates issues such as data pipeline failures, logic changes, or broken inputs, all of which can </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>negatively impact the performance of rules and models</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Dashboard Objective:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Early detection</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> of metric drift affecting fraud rules to reduce false positives, review/decline spikes, and business impact.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>What&apos;s in the Dashboard?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     A) </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' underline='true'>Metric Drift Detection Logic:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>           1. Drift Indecators:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                • </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Average Value Shift: </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>Change in Avg value over time</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                   - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Z-score &gt; 3</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                   - AND Avg % Change &gt; 50%</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                • </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Data Range Shift: </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>Change in data range over time</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                   - IQR % Change &gt; 50% -- </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>(IQR = </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>middle 50%</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'> of the data = P75 - P25)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                   - OR Spread % Change &gt; 50% -- </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>(Spread = </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>middle 80%</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'> of the data = P90 - P10)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run italic='true'>Æ     </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>           2. Drift Severity:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                • </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>High:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> Both drift indicators are met</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                • </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Medium:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> One indicator is met, with a slightly higher threshold (Z-score &gt; 4, IQR/Spread &gt; 100%)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>                • </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Low:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> One indicator is met</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     B) </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' underline='true'>Additional Info:</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' italic='true'>Supporting information to help understand the broader context and impact of drift.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>          1.</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> Rule List:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> Rules that use the metric</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>          2. </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Global Entity List:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> All global entities in which the meric is used</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>          3. </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Metric Update Info:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> Changes to the metric (e.g. new version created, version deleted/deactivated)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>          4. </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Business Impact:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>               a) </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>: Change in total friction (Decline, Review, or Approve) caused by rules using the drifted metric</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>               b) </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Share of Total Region Friction:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> The portion of total regional friction caused by rules that use the drifted metric</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     C) </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' underline='true'>Alerts:</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' italic='true'>Not every drift triggers an alert. Alerts appear only when there’s a combination of signals — either widespread drift or proven business impact.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>          Alert Types:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>               • </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Incident Alert:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                   - P0: </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>When &gt;10 metrics are flagged with </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>High</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> drift severity on the same day (region-agnostic) -- </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>Alert Message: &quot;Widespread High Metric Drift; x metrics flagged.&quot;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>                   - P1: </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>When &gt;10 metrics are flagged with </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Medium</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> drift severity on the same day (region-agnostic)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#040c28' fontsize='11'>               • </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Individual Alerts:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                  Triggers based on drift severity, rule impact, and share of region total friction -- and </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' italic='true'>only if NO Incident Alert is triggered</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                  - P0:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>High </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Drift + </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>&gt;100% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>&gt;20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> -- </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>Alert Message: &quot;High possibility of Metric Drift, High impact on rules and region’s total friction.&quot;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>                  - P1:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Medium</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> Drift +  </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>&gt;100% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>&gt;20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>                  - P2:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>High</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> drift + </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>&gt;100% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>≤20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> -- </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' italic='true'>Alert Message: &quot;High possibility of Metric Drift, High impact on rules friction, Little to no impact on region’s total friction.&quot;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>                  - P3:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Medium</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> drift + </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>&gt;200% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>≤20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>                  - P4: High</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> drift + </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>≤100% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>≤20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>                  - P5:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>Medium</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> drift + </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>≤100% Change in Rules Friction</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'> + </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='11'>≤20% of Total Region Friction</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Notes:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     1. The dashboard is </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>region-agnostic</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> — each region is evaluated independently.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     2. The current definitions and thresholds for drift signals, severity levels, and alerts are subject to change based on alignment with stakeholders.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     3. Whenever % change is mentioned here, it typically refers to a comparison between the current value and the past 7 days.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     4. We consider </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>absolute change</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>, so both increases and decreases are captured.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     5. We’ve tested multiple detection approaches with varying thresholds (Aggressive, Conservative, and More Conservative). As aligned, the current dashboard uses the </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Aggressive</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> approach. This may change with future alignment. Further details can be found here &gt;&gt;&gt; </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>(</run>
                    <run auto-url='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1icQOXH61OJyCo0CqHQAENcfWw3jyFh1-NCH8VDtsNCk/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;'>https://docs.google.com/document/d/1icQOXH61OJyCo0CqHQAENcfWw3jyFh1-NCH8VDtsNCk/edit?usp=sharing</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>)</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     6. Similarly, alerting is currently limited to </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>High drift</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> only. Therefore, for </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Incident Alerts</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>, only </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>P0</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> will appear. For </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Individual Alerts</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>, only </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>P0</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> and </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>P2</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> are shown.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>     7. Incident Alerts take precedence over Individual Alerts. For a given region and day, only one type of alert can be triggered. We first check for an Incident Alert; if none, we then check for an Individual Alert.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'><![CDATA[     8. Region here refers to the “cluster” the entity is added to in Antifraud — it doesn’t necessarily match the geographic region, or the platform name. Mapping source is <]]></run>
                    <run fontcolor='#080808' fontsize='11'>fulfillment-dwh-production.cl_fintech.antifraud_metric_definition</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>&gt;.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Source Table:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'><![CDATA[ <fulfillment-dwh-production.rl_fintech.agg_antifraud_metrics_drift_daily>]]></run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
